<title>USA: NumereX wins British Telecom contract.</title>
<headline>NumereX wins British Telecom contract.</headline>
<dateline>MEDIA, Pa. 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>NumereX Corp said Wednesday that it has signed a network equipment supply contract with British Telecommunications Plc valued at 6.8 million sterling, or about $11.4 million.</p>
<p>The agreement, said the company, establishes terms of purchase for network equipment for the quantity of equipment likely to be ordered.  As has been typical of past BT contracts, BT is not required to order any specific amount of equipment, added NumereX.</p>
<p>The contract runs through July 1999.</p>
<p>NumereX shares were trading late Thursday morning at 6-1/4.</p>
